      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">35 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Pattern primer</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Heap / Priority Queue</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Heaps and priority queues</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">A heap answers one question fast, again and again: \"what is the smallest (or largest) thing right now?\". Learn the four shapes it takes in interviews: Top-K with a size-k heap, k-way merge, scheduling with one or two heaps, and two heaps for a running median. Also learn when a heap is the wrong tool and quickselect or bucket sort wins.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Go deeper:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-two-heaps\">Two heaps and k-way merge</a>.</p>\r\n"
  },
